<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antipater</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 397–319 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antipater was a Macedonian general and statesman who served Philip II and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. After Alexander's death he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and its allies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamian-war">Lamian War</a> at Crannon in 322 BCE. He was regent of the empire from 321 BCE until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antipater.jpg" alt="Antipater" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KINGS_of_MACEDON._Alexander_III_%27the_Great%27._336-323_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
